From f33819ea403f4477f71826eb9c7bb1141ffa30a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjarne <87858321+bjakra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:43:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/kernelsu, fs: build KernelSU-Next SuSFS into the
 kernel

Compile KernelSU-Next's own SuSFS (drivers/kernelsu/susfs) into the kernelsu driver under
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS instead of loading susfs_guard_lkm.ko, which the husky kernel's forced module
signing and struct randomisation reject. SuSFS is armed from on_post_fs_data(), where ksud would
otherwise have insmod'd the module.

The only edit outside drivers/kernelsu is fs/proc/bootconfig.c: SuSFS's spoof_cmdline layer
rewrites saved_boot_config by name, so it is exposed (non-static) when CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS is set.

Generated by tools/kernel/apply-kernelsu.sh; see patches-kernel/0002-susfs.toml. SuSFS hides root
and weakens tamper detection; on because KernelSU already is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A7tdbTAv6xiqf4SbJWNdwp
